ted in cyanosulfidic systems and meteorite experiments (Patel et al., 2015). Explicitly balanced (N/C/O conserved)."}, {"id": "rxn_007", "name": "Glycolonitrile hydrolysis to glycolic acid", "inputs": ["mol_008", "mol_023", "mol_023"], "outputs": ["mol_009", "mol_001"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "300-360K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "acid/base hydrolysis"}, "mechanism": "Two-step hydrolysis: nitrile to amide (glycolamide, omitted), then acid.", "reasoning": "Explicit two-water hydrolysis of nitrile to acid plus released HCN (Ruiz-Bermejo et al., 2013; eq. balanced)."}, {"id": "rxn_008", "name": "HCN oligomerization and hydrolysis to glycine", "inputs": ["mol_001", "mol_001", "mol_001", "mol_001", "mol_003", "mol_023", "mol_023"], "outputs": ["mol_005", "mol_023", "mol_023"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "273-320K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "0.1M HCN, pH 9, then hydrolysis"}, "mechanism": "HCN tetramerization (via DAMN and oligomer), partial hydrolysis yields aminoacetonitrile (DAMN to AAN), with water as byproduct.", "reasoning": "Experimentally established for dilute HCN (Ferris et al., 1978; Ruiz-Bermejo et al., 2013). Atom balance maintained for AAN pathway."}, {"id": "rxn_009", "name": "Glyoxylate imine formation (reductive amination branch)", "inputs": ["mol_012", "mol_003"], "outputs": ["mol_014", "mol_023"], "environment": "Hydrothermal", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "320-370K", "pressure": "high", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "Alkaline, 1:1 reactant ratio"}, "mechanism": "Ammonia reacts with the carbonyl (glyoxylate) to form a hemiaminal, then dehydrates to imine.", "reasoning": "Directly supported by Paczelt et al., 2023; Barge et al., 2020; yields imine and water."}, {"id": "rxn_010", "name": "Glycine formation via Fe(II) mineral reduction (green rust/Fe